# The pc platform's Dingodile test (#1093, docs/platforms.md), played with
# --level 20 (the Dingodile fight): platform/pc/preview.keys's Start and A
# through the logos and menus to the level select (frames 1-514), which
# picks the level, then the fight, won at ~13768 (his last move,
# motion entry 3, reads gDingodileMotionRecords past its end, into the
# stalactite's records after it, as the ROM lays them out; the host's
# 16-byte alignment of that array made 36 frames of his defeat differ
# from mGBA's until boss_motion_tables.cpp's aligned(4)), the Super Body
# Slam screen and the cutscene after it, Start and A every 30 frames
# from 13900 on, then the level select again, where they start Snow
# Crash and pause it. tools/boottest.py `screens` (the same --level)
# played it on mGBA for tests/dingodile_mgba_screens.json, every 5th
# frame: all the same (every frame is).
# Written by a search over the host's runs (random moves, the ones that
# hurt Dingodile most and kept Crash alive).
# A line `FRAME KEYS` holds KEYS from FRAME on (platform/pc/src/input.c).
